WEBVTT

00:01.010 --> 00:05.060
Let's resume our battle, 
Kuzunoha the Sorcerer!

00:06.250 --> 00:07.690
<i>Huh? The sorcerer?</i>

00:08.530 --> 00:09.580
<i>That was me?!</i>

00:16.910 --> 00:21.740
I didn't want to embarrass myself 
by having to show my scales.

00:22.220 --> 00:25.260
This is your fault, too. Prepare yourself.

00:25.260 --> 00:25.990
Kuzunoha!

00:36.810 --> 00:40.550
Leave the hero and Fort Stella alone, was it?

00:40.550 --> 00:43.110
Very well. I accept your demands.

00:44.470 --> 00:47.800
<i>He's terrifying. I see why 
they call him the sorcerer.</i>

00:57.510 --> 01:00.030
It's time to actually end this.

01:01.320 --> 01:02.080
Larva-dono!

01:04.180 --> 01:09.160
You will pay for injuring my master.

01:11.420 --> 01:13.120
You don't know when to shut up.

01:35.110 --> 01:36.990
<b>Season Two</b>

02:48.100 --> 02:52.560
<b>Night Twenty-Four   Sorcerer vs. Draconid</b>

02:48.100 --> 02:52.560
<b>Night Twenty-Four   Sorcerer vs. Draconid</b>

02:52.610 --> 02:54.950
You're first.

02:54.950 --> 02:57.530
I'll begin by killing the 
sorcerer's follower.

03:17.990 --> 03:20.300
Larva-dono, dispel the mist in the area.

03:20.790 --> 03:23.640
Then we can join the fight.

03:25.110 --> 03:29.950
Hero of Limia, I am not struggling.

03:29.950 --> 03:31.930
Hah! You're ragged.

03:32.450 --> 03:35.080
Larva-dono, I'll be frank.

03:35.540 --> 03:38.570
Let me help you kill the dragon 
who destroyed the royal capital.

03:38.840 --> 03:40.500
I can't let you do that.

03:40.500 --> 03:47.580
But if you'll focus on defending, 
I'll save that mage after the battle.

03:47.580 --> 03:49.670
You, a lich?

03:49.670 --> 03:52.260
Why would an undead save the living?

03:52.260 --> 03:56.310
Really? You're sure you can save Woody?

03:56.310 --> 03:57.460
Of course.

03:57.890 --> 04:01.350
A hole in a hyuman stomach 
is easily mended.

04:03.580 --> 04:04.890
Onee-chan...

04:07.080 --> 04:09.140
I trust you.

04:09.140 --> 04:10.900
But Hibiki...

04:10.900 --> 04:12.900
No, it's the right call.

04:13.260 --> 04:15.030
O-On what basis?

04:15.030 --> 04:18.910
That lich is a lot like that 
person we met in Tsige.

04:19.560 --> 04:23.940
They keep their word. 
They seem like that kind of person.

04:25.000 --> 04:29.280
Larva-dono, you'd better 
keep your promise.

04:29.280 --> 04:31.460
Could you dismiss the mist, just in case?

04:31.900 --> 04:33.900
We have a deal.

04:34.760 --> 04:36.760
Niffelheim, dispel.

04:42.210 --> 04:44.140
Have you finished your conversation?

04:44.570 --> 04:48.040
Regardless of what you discuss, 
your efforts will be in vain.

04:48.040 --> 04:51.930
Now, allow me to destroy 
you with my true swords.

04:53.680 --> 04:58.800
Lancer the blade dragon. 
Dragon of swords and people.

04:58.800 --> 05:01.860
An unusual creature who possesses two lives.

05:01.860 --> 05:03.580
You know about that?

05:03.900 --> 05:09.580
Despite being a dragon, you take on a 
humanoid form and enhance your strength.

05:09.580 --> 05:12.990
I see. Luto-dono's words 
were quite accurate.

05:13.560 --> 05:14.530
Luto?

05:14.810 --> 05:17.170
How do you know that name?

05:17.170 --> 05:22.100
Surrounded by numerous fine swords, you are 
the greater dragon known as Mitsurugi.

05:22.100 --> 05:27.380
Those swords speak to the fate of 
the warriors who challenged you.

05:27.900 --> 05:30.350
You know too much.

05:30.350 --> 05:33.020
I can't allow you to live.

05:33.330 --> 05:35.920
I will add you to my power!

05:36.770 --> 05:39.880
I dress myself in grievances.

05:41.030 --> 05:42.640
Gross Shear.

05:44.060 --> 05:47.070
The swaying silver cage deflects arrows.

05:47.350 --> 05:48.520
Marugiri!

05:54.960 --> 05:58.130
You held out against my true swords?

05:58.130 --> 06:01.600
I have done my research on you, Lancer,

06:01.600 --> 06:05.090
with help from Luto-dono, 
leader of the dragons.

06:06.160 --> 06:09.340
I wasn't expecting a lich with ties to Luto.

06:09.340 --> 06:14.390
I believe the greatest weapon 
people possess is their intellect.

06:14.390 --> 06:17.170
Of course, I am only a former person.

06:18.390 --> 06:23.720
Worthy of the sixth self, 
release the whip and become a blade.

06:23.720 --> 06:24.890
Ascaron!

06:26.840 --> 06:28.810
Aren't you a mage?

06:28.810 --> 06:33.100
This is Ascaron, a blade steeped 
in poison and curses.

06:33.100 --> 06:35.680
Hoping I'd get to kill you someday,

06:35.680 --> 06:39.760
I named it after another sword 
known as a dragon slayer.

06:40.150 --> 06:42.400
All it does is give off an ominous air.

06:42.400 --> 06:44.840
It lacks the gleam of a truly fine blade.

06:45.160 --> 06:48.790
No matter. I am the one wielding it.

06:48.790 --> 06:50.800
Fine blades do not suit me.

06:51.500 --> 06:54.270
Release the sixth step, Flay.

06:55.010 --> 06:57.010
Sword Spiritem!

06:58.640 --> 07:01.060
So you're determined to use that?

07:01.490 --> 07:04.850
You're a foolish mage to 
challenge me with a sword.

07:06.390 --> 07:08.330
This is the battlefield.

07:08.790 --> 07:12.590
The capital's best soldiers and the 
strongest demons are all over the place.

07:12.590 --> 07:15.800
I'm sure many of them will add to my power.

07:16.160 --> 07:19.810
How long can you keep fighting back?

07:22.810 --> 07:27.790
You'd challenge Ascaron with that 
rabble's swords? Laughable.

07:27.790 --> 07:31.500
It's time you experienced fear.

07:39.350 --> 07:41.190
Well? Did that hurt?

07:41.660 --> 07:44.310
Y-You'll pay for that!

07:44.310 --> 07:48.100
I heard you severed my master's fingers.

07:48.100 --> 07:49.900
This is what you get for that!

07:53.780 --> 07:58.070
Are these the swords once 
wielded by past heroes?

07:58.070 --> 08:00.130
That's not all!

08:08.180 --> 08:11.510
What's the matter? I am a mage.

08:11.820 --> 08:13.890
This shouldn't shock you.

08:21.370 --> 08:24.050
Pierce the brilliance of vitality.

08:24.050 --> 08:25.300
Stare Celot!

08:25.300 --> 08:27.410
You're chanting incantations 
between strikes?

08:27.410 --> 08:29.900
My sword returns to me on its own.

08:30.320 --> 08:31.940
Rot Counter!

08:31.940 --> 08:33.680
Don't underestimate me!

08:40.300 --> 08:45.430
You won't be able to count how many 
I break before your destruction.

08:46.170 --> 08:48.800
<i>This is thanks to the three 
of them training me.</i>

08:49.700 --> 08:52.540
<i>I wouldn't have been strong enough before.</i>

08:55.670 --> 08:59.690
<i>For the young master's sake, as well 
as my own, I cannot disgrace myself.</i>

09:00.110 --> 09:04.790
Damn it. How could I be defeated not by 
the sorcerer himself, but by his follower?

09:04.790 --> 09:08.860
<i>Ascaron's poison is slowly consuming him.</i>

09:09.310 --> 09:12.320
<i>All his reactions are slowing.</i>

09:12.740 --> 09:17.200
<i>I pray you don't notice. 
May you die in despair.</i>

09:29.520 --> 09:33.200
Heroes, become my strength!

09:37.060 --> 09:38.150
Chiya!

09:44.760 --> 09:46.330
Sealy-san...

09:46.740 --> 09:48.870
Damn. I missed.

09:48.870 --> 09:50.690
<i>Thank you, adventurer.</i>

09:51.340 --> 09:55.790
<i>If that priestess had become a sword, 
I probably would've lost.</i>

09:56.800 --> 09:59.320
I wasn't expecting to go out like this...

10:01.960 --> 10:03.330
It can't be helped.

10:03.330 --> 10:06.430
Though you don't compare 
to the hero or priestess,

10:06.430 --> 10:08.580
I shall use you as part of my power.

10:08.890 --> 10:10.240
Sealy-san!

10:10.240 --> 10:10.950
Damn it!

10:10.950 --> 10:14.960
I haven't felt this cornered 
since I fought Sofia.

10:14.960 --> 10:19.290
You will surely make a good 
sword and serve me well.

10:19.290 --> 10:21.460
Who would serve you?

10:21.460 --> 10:25.100
I've already found a master to serve!

10:31.860 --> 10:34.480
See that, sorcerer's follower?

10:34.480 --> 10:38.750
This is the might of one who rules over 
dragons and the natural law of—

10:44.620 --> 10:46.590
Wh-Who is that?

10:46.990 --> 10:50.570
I'm ashamed to admit it, but this 
is the most I can manage right now.

10:51.170 --> 10:53.010
<i>I used my lich appearance as a decoy</i>

10:53.010 --> 10:55.990
<i>for a desperate attack with 
Ascaron from his blind spot.</i>

10:55.990 --> 10:57.840
<i>That was a close call.</i>

10:57.840 --> 10:59.090
<i>I need more training.</i>

10:59.480 --> 11:01.470
Wh-Who are you?

11:01.870 --> 11:04.420
Is that you, Larva-dono?

11:04.420 --> 11:05.320
<i>What?!</i>

11:05.320 --> 11:06.380
<i>Huh? No way.</i>

11:06.380 --> 11:09.200
<i>So the otherworlder figured it out.</i>

11:09.690 --> 11:12.840
People don't normally notice so easily.

11:13.490 --> 11:17.910
Including my failures up to this point, 
I'm dealing with quite the headache.

11:17.910 --> 11:21.070
What does this mean? Were you 
actually a hyuman all along?

11:21.510 --> 11:24.040
A very long time ago.

11:24.360 --> 11:27.490
Now, a promise is a promise.

11:28.550 --> 11:31.550
Release the fifth step, Keto.

11:34.840 --> 11:37.680
Agatoram, heal him.

11:43.850 --> 11:45.270
His color is returning!

11:45.270 --> 11:49.640
That should be enough. 
All he needs now is rest.

11:49.640 --> 11:51.550
Thank you.

11:52.460 --> 11:57.770
Larva-dono, I swear on my name that 
I will repay this debt someday.

11:57.770 --> 11:59.650
I'll think about it.

11:59.650 --> 12:04.350
<i>I overused my rings this time. 
I must rest for a while.</i>

12:04.350 --> 12:05.260
Wait.

12:05.810 --> 12:09.850
Is it true that you're the sorcerer's follower?

12:09.850 --> 12:14.660
Forget about that. A hero has 
other things to attend to first.

12:15.140 --> 12:19.180
The citizens who have already evacuated 
must be trembling with anxiety.

12:19.680 --> 12:23.640
There's plenty you should deal with 
before concerning yourself with me.

12:25.250 --> 12:27.480
You're right.

12:28.500 --> 12:32.070
Like Verda said, someday I'll repay you.

12:32.070 --> 12:34.200
I'll keep that in mind.

12:37.960 --> 12:40.920
Hibiki, we should let Woody rest first.

12:40.920 --> 12:44.540
Once we get outside the city, 
we may be able to find a few camps.

12:44.540 --> 12:45.100
Right.

12:45.820 --> 12:50.710
<i>The sorcerer's cosplay suit must be 
connected to my former world somehow.</i>

12:50.710 --> 12:52.080
<i>And...</i>

12:52.320 --> 12:57.030
By the way, did you purchase that sword from 
the Kuzunoha Trading Company in Tsige?

12:57.470 --> 13:02.820
<i>It's possible they're connected to 
the Kuzunoha Trading Company.</i>

13:09.980 --> 13:12.010
What? Did your mind break?

13:12.510 --> 13:16.360
No. I've got two things to laugh about.

13:17.050 --> 13:18.070
Uh-huh.

13:18.070 --> 13:19.220
The first is...

13:19.720 --> 13:22.920
No matter how long you've 
been with a partner,

13:22.920 --> 13:26.280
they always die so 
disappointingly and easily.

13:26.720 --> 13:28.680
So Lancer is dead.

13:29.100 --> 13:30.730
The other is...

13:31.000 --> 13:33.760
how astonished I am with my own good luck.

13:34.160 --> 13:36.870
I seem to have won our bet.

13:36.870 --> 13:38.950
You mean a bet with Lancer?

13:38.950 --> 13:43.720
Yes. If I died first, I'd join his collection.

13:43.720 --> 13:48.720
If he died first, he'd give me 
his remaining life and power.

13:49.080 --> 13:51.680
That's the bet we made.

13:55.220 --> 13:59.720
Remaining life? So Lancer 
had more than one life.

13:59.720 --> 14:03.040
But what can you hope to 
accomplish now that it's yours?

14:03.350 --> 14:07.660
Looking down on your opponent 
during a fight sure is disgusting.

14:08.320 --> 14:11.030
I've done it often myself. 
I should reflect on my actions.

14:11.300 --> 14:12.570
Should you?

14:12.570 --> 14:18.950
Isn't it the law of the battlefield 
that the strong do as they please?

14:19.480 --> 14:25.700
I'll show you my trump card that 
overpowered and slew two greater dragons.

14:32.080 --> 14:34.870
Are we in a separate space?

14:35.850 --> 14:38.850
Welcome to the prison of swords.

14:38.850 --> 14:44.070
It's a special space connected to 
where Lancer stores his swords.

14:44.070 --> 14:47.400
It's also an execution site.

14:47.400 --> 14:52.860
Wow. You've got all these swords and 
dragged me into a separate space.

14:52.860 --> 14:55.340
With rare exceptions, 
it's hardly ever happened to me.

14:55.340 --> 14:58.420
The service here is excellent, 
so don't worry.

14:58.420 --> 15:00.980
I promise you won't be bored.

15:00.980 --> 15:02.800
I'm looking forward to that.

15:04.740 --> 15:07.120
I see.

15:07.770 --> 15:11.820
This space enhances the power 
of the one who deploys it.

15:11.820 --> 15:13.220
Pretty standard.

15:13.220 --> 15:17.230
Wait, and... it shares existence 
and ownership with the swords?

15:18.020 --> 15:19.670
How do you know all that?

15:20.310 --> 15:23.660
That clearly wasn't a flash of brilliance.

15:24.970 --> 15:29.890
Oh, I get it. All these swords are your lives.

15:30.420 --> 15:34.620
By acquiring their swords, you also inherit 
the skills the heroes had in life.

15:34.990 --> 15:38.250
You've gone for not only 
quantity, but quality, as well.

15:39.070 --> 15:42.830
Knowing that won't help you 
against the prison of swords.

15:42.830 --> 15:49.760
I'm disappointed you used such 
boring abilities until the very end.

15:50.250 --> 15:52.410
Kuzunoha, what is...

15:53.020 --> 15:56.340
I'm not a warrior or a mage.

15:56.810 --> 16:00.960
I'm something else entirely, Sofia. 
I'm actually...

16:01.480 --> 16:02.830
a kyudoka.

16:11.790 --> 16:13.790
Bastard!

16:15.990 --> 16:18.910
<i>She's hitting way harder now.</i>

16:20.910 --> 16:23.500
<i>To be safe, I'll strengthen 
it with my kai.</i>

16:27.120 --> 16:28.060
Wha—

16:28.060 --> 16:30.330
This weapon's name is Azusa.

16:30.330 --> 16:33.420
I named it after the ancient azusa yumi.

16:33.830 --> 16:36.890
Since I've got some mildly 
dangerous whistling arrows,

16:36.890 --> 16:39.550
I think I'll go with an exorcism.

16:40.020 --> 16:41.560
Don't!

16:50.620 --> 16:54.360
Th-This wasn't supposed 
to happen! You monster!

16:54.860 --> 16:59.520
What... What are you?!

16:59.830 --> 17:04.200
Like I said, I'm a kyudoka.

17:09.140 --> 17:12.550
But I haven't even met Luto yet.

17:15.850 --> 17:17.850
I can't die.

17:18.800 --> 17:20.710
Don't make me laugh.

17:20.710 --> 17:24.730
I can't believe you don't even realize 
you're being used as a camera.

17:25.620 --> 17:30.100
I'd feel sorry if you died with my fake 
name in your heart, so I'll tell you.

17:30.690 --> 17:34.060
My real name is Misumi Makoto.

17:35.940 --> 17:38.700
Goodbye, Sofia Bulga.

17:40.810 --> 17:43.100
N-No! There's still more!

17:44.690 --> 17:49.080
Damn you for keeping secrets 
until the end, Lancer!

17:49.610 --> 17:53.840
I'm not over yet! I can't end yet!

17:59.620 --> 18:00.760
A Japanese sword?

18:01.910 --> 18:05.740
I actually don't mind risking it all.

18:06.320 --> 18:08.830
<i>Lancer's secret weapon?</i>

18:08.830 --> 18:11.780
<i>If they were a hero who turned 
into a Japanese sword...</i>

18:12.290 --> 18:15.400
<i>Does that mean they were Japanese? A sage?</i>

18:15.690 --> 18:18.170
This sword is amazing.

18:18.170 --> 18:22.910
Despite lacking a signature and being 
incomplete, it fills me with power.

18:22.910 --> 18:25.340
It feels different from absorbing a dragon.

18:25.340 --> 18:28.130
It's like evolving into a next-level human.

18:28.500 --> 18:30.280
<i>A next-level human?</i>

18:30.280 --> 18:33.000
<i>Isn't that what Shiki was 
previously trying to become?</i>

18:33.390 --> 18:35.150
<i>A grant, was it?</i>

18:40.390 --> 18:42.520
I can hardly believe how much 
I struggled to get here.

18:42.860 --> 18:44.680
The tables have turned.

18:45.310 --> 18:48.050
It's what I'd expect from a Japanese sword.

18:48.790 --> 18:50.490
Now it's all about speed.

18:52.000 --> 18:54.430
I'll go with archery, not kyudo.

18:55.680 --> 18:58.140
Fantasy style.

19:25.060 --> 19:28.270
Luto, you owe me one.

19:46.760 --> 19:49.530
That just leaves Fort Stella.

19:49.930 --> 19:52.510
<i>That said, I'd better watch my line of fire.</i>

19:53.490 --> 19:56.450
<i>Apparently I'm responsible 
for creating Star Lake.</i>

19:57.550 --> 19:59.420
Around here should do.

19:59.770 --> 20:01.200
<i>Oh, mana matter!</i>

20:01.200 --> 20:02.420
<i>When it comes to convenience,</i>

20:02.420 --> 20:03.550
<i>nothing can beat it.</i>

20:04.420 --> 20:07.100
<i>I'll expand my kai to maximum size</i>

20:07.100 --> 20:10.250
<i>and focus on determining the 
topography and situation.</i>

20:14.710 --> 20:17.820
<i>Good. Rona had her soldiers evacuate.</i>

20:18.410 --> 20:24.160
<i>I don't know the exact distance, 
but I doubt I'll miss.</i>

20:33.310 --> 20:36.190
All right! I've completed 
the goddess's request.

20:36.190 --> 20:38.660
That settles that matter.

20:42.060 --> 20:45.700
I've completely gotten used to falling.

20:50.490 --> 20:51.890
Now, then...

20:52.620 --> 20:54.220
Young Master!

20:54.220 --> 20:56.970
Huh? Shiki, your face is visible.

20:58.280 --> 21:02.760
I'm sorry. Surprisingly, I had some trouble.

21:02.760 --> 21:05.290
The hero escaped safely, though.

21:05.290 --> 21:06.770
I see. That's good, then.

21:07.280 --> 21:12.360
I was able to determine my current 
strength, but I'm pretty tired.

21:12.360 --> 21:13.670
Let's get out of here quickly.

21:14.470 --> 21:16.630
Are you sure?

21:16.990 --> 21:19.870
You seemed to recognize the hero.

21:20.690 --> 21:25.240
I know her, but we'll discuss 
that once we're back.

21:25.720 --> 21:28.750
Tomoe and Mio are probably 
back at the demiplane, too.

21:28.750 --> 21:35.040
By the way, the hero's party said they 
wanted to thank me when I rescued them.

21:35.040 --> 21:37.090
What shall we ask for?

21:37.970 --> 21:39.570
I'll think about it.

21:40.190 --> 21:43.250
I'm sure they're busy with the city right now.

21:43.250 --> 21:44.560
Understood.

21:46.190 --> 21:52.970
<i>Limia will struggle in the future, 
but they have Senpai.</i>

21:53.760 --> 21:57.260
<i>I'm sure she can manage most things.</i>

21:57.670 --> 22:00.910
Shall we head home?

22:00.910 --> 22:01.720
Yes.

23:35.240 --> 23:37.060
Night Twenty-Five,

23:35.390 --> 23:39.930
<b>Next Time</b>

23:36.980 --> 23:39.930
<b>Party Beneath the Moonlight</b>

23:37.060 --> 23:38.800
"Party Beneath the Moonlight."
